+#### [LexNLP](https://github.com/LexPredict/lexpredict-lexnlp)
+> **Description:** LexNLP is one of the older and still relevant legal NLP libraries for extracting information from real, unstructured legal text. The README covers sentence parsing aware of legal abbreviations, models for legal concepts, classifiers for document and clause types, and extractors for monetary amounts, dates, courts, regulations, and citations. It is not a turnkey law-firm app, but it is a strong toolkit for building clause extraction, contract analytics, and legal text parsing systems. **GitHub stats:** 753 stars, Jupyter Notebook, AGPL-3.0. **Last GitHub activity surfaced during research:** 2024-05-27.
