+
+> This curated list of the best AI tools for lawyers in 2026 focuses only on open source projects that exist as public GitHub repositories. It is built for legal teams that want self-hosted, inspectable tooling for contract review, legal research, OCR, redaction, annotation, document intelligence, and knowledge retrieval without relying on proprietary SaaS lock-in.
