+> **Description:** OCRmyPDF adds an OCR text layer to scanned PDFs while preserving the source file structure and producing searchable output. The README highlights multi-language OCR, deskewing, rotation fixes, PDF/A output, metadata control, and command-line batchability. For lawyers dealing with scanned exhibits, court filings, discovery productions, or closing binders, this is one of the highest-value utility repos in the ecosystem because it turns dead PDFs into searchable inputs for downstream AI. **GitHub stats:** 32.0k stars, Python, MPL-2.0. **Last GitHub activity surfaced during research:** 2025-12-15.
